	(text "SD CARD SHIELD - deliberately NOT grounded (design review: \"don't ground shields\").\nJ4 pin SH carries a no-connect flag. Grounding a card-cage shell at the schematic level forces\nit onto the digital ground net, which turns the shell into a return path for card-slot noise and\ncan inject it straight into the SDMMC bus. Leave the decision to layout: bring the shell pad out\nas an isolated pad with a 0R / stitching-cap footprint next to it, and populate only if EMC\ntesting asks for it. The USB-C shell on J2 IS still grounded - that one is correct, a USB-C\nreceptacle shell is meant to be bonded for cable-shield continuity.\n\nSD CLOCK - \"homework: find out SD protocol clock speed\"\n  SDMMC1 kernel clock = 125 MHz (PLL1Q) in the CubeMX config.\n  SD bus modes:  Default Speed 25 MHz | High Speed 50 MHz | SDR104 208 MHz (UHS-I, needs 1.8V)\n  This board is 3.3V only, so the UHS modes are out and 50 MHz is the hard ceiling.\n  SDMMC divider:  f = 125 / (2 x CLKDIV)\n     CLKDIV = 0  -> 125   MHz   bypass, far too fast\n     CLKDIV = 1  ->  62.5 MHz   TOO FAST (over the 50 MHz ceiling)\n     CLKDIV = 2  ->  31.25 MHz  <- High Speed, safe, this is the target\n     CLKDIV = 3  ->  20.8  MHz\n  Bring up at 25 MHz (Default Speed), then move to CLKDIV=2 / 31.25 MHz.\n  4-bit wide at 31.25 MHz = 125 Mbit/s = ~15.6 MB/s raw.\n  R10-R14 (47k) are the bus pull-ups the SD spec requires on DAT0-3 and CMD; R15 (10k) pulls\n  the card-detect line up. CLK is the one SDMMC line that must NOT be pulled up.\n  Layout: keep all six bus traces length-matched and short - at 31.25 MHz the edges matter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.02 271.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "de7deed6-216b-4d2a-9ae1-2702dd9e9335")
	)
